<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia c/account deficit widens in Oct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia c/account deficit widens in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally-adjusted current account deficit widened to A$1.788 billion in October from September's deficit of A$1.690 billion, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This compares with a seasonally adjusted deficit of A$2.125 billion in October 1995.</p>
<p>The unadjusted October deficit was A$2.367 billion against A$2.229 billion in September, compared with a deficit of A$2.543 billion in October 1995.</p>
<p>Economists had on average forecast a seasonally adjusted October current account deficit of about A$1.60 billion.  </p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJ	  Oct 96     Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p>    Current account    -1.788 bln  -1.690 bln   -2.125 bln</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -21 million     -15 million	-83 million</p>
<p>    Exports		 6.302 bln   6.227 bln    5.995 bln</p>
<p>    Imports		 6.323 bln   6.242 bln    6.078 bln</p>
<p>    Net Services	    +12 million     -11 million	-37 million</p>
<p>    Goods/services	   -9 million     -26 million     -120 million</p>
<p>    Net income	   -1.910 bln  -1.759 bln   -2.094 bln</p>
<p>    Net unreq transfers  +131 million     +95 million	+89 million</p>
<p>    UNADJUSTED		Oct 96     Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p>NET CAPITAL TRANSACTIONS</p>
<p>    Gen govt	     +1.687 bln    -365 million   +1.916 bln</p>
<p>    Reserve Bank	 +1.236 bln    -397 million	-62 million</p>
<p>    Total official     +2.923 bln    -762 million   +1.854 bln</p>
<p>Non-official capital</p>
<p>    balancing item	 -557 million  +2.991 bln     +689 million</p>
<p>The Bureau said exports rose one percent in October, seasonally adjusted, with rural exports falling four percent and non-rural exports rising three percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
